# Development Workflow & Deployment

## Environment Setup

- Requires Node.js 22+ (specified in [package.json](mdc:package.json))
- Use pnpm as package manager (`corepack enable` to enable)
- Environment variables: `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` for Redis API gateway

## Development Commands

- `pnpm dev` - Start development server with Turbopack
- `pnpm build` - Create production build
- `pnpm start -- -p 10050` - Serve production build on port 10050
- `pnpm lint` - Run ESLint checks
- `pnpm format` - Apply Prettier formatting
- `pnpm format:check` - Verify Prettier formatting

## PM2 Deployment

- PM2 ecosystem config in [eco.config.js](mdc:eco.config.js)
- Commands: `pm2:start`, `pm2:stop`, `pm2:restart`, `pm2:delete`, `pm2:logs`, `pm2:monit`
- Production deployment: `pnpm pm2:start` (includes git pull, build, and PM2 start)

## Testing & Quality Assurance

- No formal test suite yet - manual QA required
- Document manual testing steps in PRs
- Future tests should use React Testing Library/Playwright
- Test files should follow `*.test.tsx` pattern in `src/**/__tests__/`

## Git & Commit Guidelines

- Follow `type: summary` commit message format
- Types: feat, fix, refactor, chore, docs, style, perf, test, build
- Keep commit messages concise and imperative
- Pull requests should include screenshots for UI changes
- Reference spec sections or issues in PRs
